      "trace_interpretation": "The trace is a candidate syscall superset and requires later on-device negative testing; it is not attempted in this unit."
    },
    {
      "item": "dropbear-argv-flag-semantics",
      "reason": "The launch argv is bound as an exact token sequence, but each flag's meaning is not yet bound against the selected Dropbear version. The design requires that a runtime option is accepted only after its exact selected-version source/help/parser semantics are independently bound. The bound sequence includes -a alongside the -j and -k forwarding denials, and that combination is not yet justified from source.",
      "successor_method": "After the private pinned Dropbear source arrives, derive each flag's meaning from that exact version's option parser, record a per-flag semantics table beside the argv, and reject or replace any flag whose effect is not required by the session contract."
    },
    {
      "item": "seccomp-positive-syscall-argument-allowlist",
      "reason": "It derives from the exact PID-1, Dropbear, dispatcher, and workload service trace, which is not available until the deferred Dropbear build and all binaries are materialized.",
      "successor_method": "Run qemu-aarch64 user-mode tracing after the binaries are built; treat the output as a candidate superset and later perform on-device negative testing."
    },
    {
      "item": "capability-minimum-set",
      "reason": "The exact minimum must be derived from the same service trace and native bootstrap boundary; it is not invented from a static guess here.",
      "successor_method": "Derive from the completed trace and independently review before any candidate."
    },
    {
      "item": "proc-scalar-allowlist",
      "reason": "The exact scalar reads are consumer-dependent and cannot be selected before the completed service trace.",
      "successor_method": "Derive from the completed trace, bind a finite read-only list, and independently review before any candidate."
    }
